      "topicId": "math-y9-changing-subject",
      "stem": "For integer x from 0 to 100, let $y=(3x-2)/5$ and $z=(2x+6)/4$. Both y and z must be integers and $-3\\le z-y\\le-1$. Which option correctly makes x the subject of y and gives the sum T of all qualifying x?",
